      "`LocaleRoot` (`@jgengine/react`): The shell's locale root: keeps `i18n` on the player's locale setting (browser default, base-locale fallback), provides it to the tree, and sets `lang` and `dir` on the document and a wrapper so right-to-left locales flip the HUD. Also `LocaleScope`, `TextDirectionProvider`, `useTextDirection`.",
      "`bun run games:provision build <game>` runs a game's asset pipeline in one call: provision, KTX2 texture twins, simplified mesh levels and baked impostor atlases for the model files its `jgengine.json` `assetBuild` names. Cached by content, at most 4 workers, idle priority; `--no-impostors` and `--textures-only` narrow it.",
      "`buildModelLods` (`@jgengine/assets`) writes `<file>.lods/` beside a model: geometry-only levels that keep each material's source index, an optional impostor atlas, and `meta.json`.",
      "`visibility.meshLods: { screenSizes, hysteresis?, impostorDistance? }` switches props and scatter to the built levels by size on screen, and big props to baked impostor cards past a distance. `ModelConfig.meshLods` overrides it per model; `false` turns it off. Off unless set; a model with no built files draws as before.",
      "`ModelVariantLodConfig` takes `hysteresisRatio` and `scaleWithInstance`.",
      "Harbor Heat builds levels for its library props and trees and bakes impostors for its jacaranda and quiver trees; Fernwild builds levels for its grass, flowers, plants, mushrooms and ore rocks.",
      "`CharacterMotion` (`@jgengine/core/physics/physicsBackend`): A backend-native kinematic character mover: collide-and-slide, stepping, slopes and ground snap in the solver. Also `CharacterMotionDesc`, `CharacterMotionResult`, `PhysicsQuatOut`, `PhysicsVec3Out`, `RayCastVehicle`, `RayCastVehicleDesc`, `RayCastWheelDesc`, `RayCastWheelState`.",
      "`VehicleBackendLinkState` (`@jgengine/core/physics/vehicleBackendLink`): A link's serializable state: the pose its chassis last synced to.",
      "`DEFAULT_SIM_HZ` (`@jgengine/core/runtime/simLoop`): Steps per second a loop runs at when `hz` is not set: the physics backends' own substep rate, so one sim step is one solver step.",
      "`RapierSnapshot` (`@jgengine/rapier`): A Rapier backend's serializable state: the world bytes plus the engine-handle tables over Rapier's own handles.",
      "`RapierSnapshot` (`@jgengine/rapier/rapierBackend`): A Rapier backend's serializable state: the world bytes plus the engine-handle tables over Rapier's own handles.",
      "`defineGame({ health })` (`@jgengine/shell`) turns on crash reports, telemetry, auto quality and the game's own recoverable error screen. Each part is off unless the game sets it, and no vendor SDK is in the engine.",
      "`createCrashSeam`, `installCrashHandlers` and `scrubCrashText` (`@jgengine/core/health/crashSeam`) catch render, tick and async errors, window errors and unhandled rejections, and hand a scrubbed report with build, game, tier and the last N events to an injected `CrashReporter`.",
      "`createTelemetry` (`@jgengine/core/health/telemetrySink`) is a batched, bounded event queue in front of an injected `TelemetrySink`; with no sink it does nothing.",
      "`createAutoQuality` (`@jgengine/core/health/autoQuality`) picks a graphics tier from frame time with hysteresis, a cooldown and backoff, driven by an injected clock. A new Auto quality setting keeps the player's tier pick and every effect toggle.",
      "Per-game `bundleKb` budgets in each game's `perf-budget.json`, enforced and printed as a table by the site asset check.",
      "The load probe reports bytes allocated per tick under `BUN_JSC_useGC=false`.",
      "Drift Foundry turns on auto quality and its own error screen.",
      "`createWorldStreamer` follows every focus point (every player), with hysteresis, per-update load and unload budgets, a loading state held until `markReady`, `retune`, and `snapshot`/`restore`. `gridShards` and `gridCellId` make streamed grid cells.",
      "`createCellContent` (`@jgengine/core/visibility/cellContent`), with `sceneObjectCells` and `sceneEntityCells`: bodies and entities in an unloaded cell keep simulating, freeze, or despawn with a saved record, by the rule the game picks, and come back a few per tick.",
      "`createCellStreaming` and `bindCellStreaming` (`@jgengine/core/visibility/cellStreaming`): cells load and unload around every player within budgets, and model files are fetched before a cell's content comes back. The renderer keeps an away cell's far proxy, parks a leaving cell once its proxy is built, and warms cells it has never seen.",
      "`createNavTiles` and `navTileFromGrid` (`@jgengine/core/nav/navTiles`): a nav mesh built and stored per tile, rebuilt only where a region changed, streamed around focus points, and stitched into one `NavRuntime` so paths cross tile borders.",
      "`ObjectStore.retain` keeps parked props in `snapshot()`, so a save written while a cell is away still holds them.",
