      "first-order glaciers match each face's speed to the first-order solve, so a smooth steep bed carries a smooth ice surface (steps under 2 m, from 130–150 m)",
      "the editor's Asset library 'Add to game' and drag work in the shared dev runner (bun run drive): the runner serves library pulls for the game it hosts, and the pulled files join that game's asset list",
      "a game quoting a makehuman: key gets it at provision time",
      "round state and agent work schedules run on the shared phase part; a finished match no longer reports a full timeLeft",
      "Fernwild's from-zero proof faces what it gathers, closes a tame's inventory opened by mistake, rests when winded, walks to the Phiomia itself and stops chopping before the bag is overweight",
      "a grass field's ground mat samples the ground once per vertex instead of six times, and tests only the clearance masks that reach it, so large grass fields no longer freeze the click into play",
      "Wet fuel no longer catches when lit; a cell's fire only starts where its fuel can carry one.",
      "the browser fixture cleanup test holds its save response without a real socket, so it no longer times out on Linux CI",
      "event, break, combo and resource meters, regen shields, vitals and body temperature run on the shared meter, pool and tier parts; stat modifiers stack through statGraph; reward claims use pickUniform",
      "round state and agent work schedules run on the shared phase part; a finished match no longer reports a full timeLeft",
      "quest, skill tree, talent, recipe and build permission gates are conditions the shared requirement part evaluates; harvest strikes use spatial/spatialIndex instead of their own grid",
      "wave countdowns and population refills run on the shared schedule part; spawn picks, wave entries and population species use the shared weighted pick; pressure and interest tiers use tierAt",
      "affixes, loot stats and walk speed stack through statGraph; encumbrance tiers use tierAt; loot plans and Scrap Signal's rarity roll use pickWeighted",
      "glacial erosion as the square of sliding speed (erosionExponent 2) no longer runs away; a valley comes out the same whether 16 kyr pass in one landscape step or eight",
      "ice and bed take turns within a landscape step, each turn wearing at most a tenth of a cell and at least iceStep long, and walls the ice undercuts collapse after each turn",
      "till piles no higher than the ice it melts out of and no steeper than its angle of repose, takes the room of the ice that held it, and what runs clear of the ice leaves with the meltwater",
      "loose cover under a glacier is held by the ice and does not slide",
      "debris a glacier melts out emerges on its surface and rides to where the ice ends, laid there as end and lateral moraines instead of a till blanket under the glacier that shielded its bed",
      "a sugar maple grows from seed to 400 years in about 3.6 s, down from 6.4 s. Passes are fused, the growth solve walks only nodes with spare sapwood, the bud threshold uses a quickselect, and the light field and pipe cost are classes so many live plants stay fast",
      "old crowns no longer freeze at the bud cap and starve. Leaf cohorts keep their age through merges, gas exchange keeps half its rate at the height limit (Koch et al. 2004), and lateral tips that keep losing at the cap give their slot away (Sachs & Novoplansky 1995)",
      "short grass (greens, fairways) showed no blades because the turf mat floated above them; the mat now sits under the blades and carries fine blade grain and normal detail up close",
      "a small grass patch with no mow stripes lost its whole mat to the edge feather",
      "survey outlines (coast, ridge, river, biome) no longer draw as brown road strips across the ground and the shallows",
