      "Fernwild owns its baby-to-adult stages, timings, incubation bands and litter odds; old breeding saves start fresh (save key fernwild.breeding2)",
      "the night sky stayed dusk-orange. Night now holds between the twilights, and the day cycle owns fog colour, so night has no bright horizon band.",
      "Fernwild, Scrap Signal and Beacon Bastion own their boss costs, caps, clocks and phase numbers; old Fernwild boss saves start fresh (save key fernwild.brood)",
      "Fernwild owns its taming numbers and food rows in data/taming.ts; old creature saves start fresh (save key fernwild.creatures2)",
      "weather particles, lightning, fire smoke, reverb noise, scatter regions, editor directives, world-model schedule chances, LOD phases and building massing now draw from the shared generator, so their seeded output changes once. Terrain shape, llmville rolls and harbor-heat traffic keep their exact values.",
      "A 403 saying the session's GitHub access is not enabled is reported as a sandbox policy denial naming the entry, not as a transient error.",
      "the crowd and RVO hot paths measure length with math/scalar length2 (sqrt of the squares) instead of Math.hypot, so the nav crowd corridor test reads the same gap on every machine (from #2846, with clamp's doc comment restored)",
      "CI's core test shard ran 1,000 files in one process for about 13 minutes on every PR; the long simulation tests move to shard d, and shards d and h run in four cost-balanced lanes",
      "preflight runs only the generators a diff reaches, and skips one whose inputs have not changed since it last ran; a lane never fails on a stale generated file, and a stale api baseline entry is pruned at land time",
      "CI's full-history checkouts fetch no file contents up front, and the games job type-checks the reached games four at a time",
      "a test that reads the wall clock runs alone after its shard's lanes, so a timing budget never measures the tests beside it",
      "`jgengine has` ranks by names first, drops description-only hits, names the parts a feature is made of and answers `gap` below the bar",
      "The builder template binds no pause key, since it has no game-flow pause.",
      "breeding is built from the Inheritance and Phases parts; a dog breeds with only those two imported; game/breeding.ts is gone and Fernwild's stage list lives in its config",
      "the last private clamp and lerp copies in core use the math home; bounds are ordered at the call sites that could reverse them",
      "the boot probe, load guard and captures launch Chromium headless with no sandbox when the machine has no display, so a cloud landing needs no Xvfb",
      "resource ledger bands and decay meter thresholds are the Ladder part",
      "Received-damage scale, flat, cap and floor policies fold through the stat ops.",
      "Vital and decay rates scale through `applyStatRate`; a rate may now be a stack of named stat-op contributions.",
      "Loot filter rules, standing requirements, upgrade standing gates and unlock gates are predicates.",
      "every private clamp, lerp and clamp01 copy in core is deleted; the homes are math/scalar and anim/easing",
      "resource nodes refill through the Slots part and the creature, driver and traffic cooldowns run on the Schedule part",
      "every weighted choice in core goes through random/pick pickWeighted; the private weight loops in city, roads, storyteller, decisionGraph and spatialSample are gone",
      "Ember Command roads use `ground/dirt-road` instead of packed dirt, and cliffs use `ground/cliff` instead of Rock022's `ground/rock`.",
      "Brightway Park looks like its art direction: Quaternius guests and staff, town pieces in place of boxes, food props on stalls, its sky, grade, fonts and paper kit, and credits for the new packs",
      "Deepward looks like its art direction: authored machinery in place of primitive props, its sky, grade, fonts and terminal kit, its own menu, settings and credits",
      "Drift Foundry looks like its art direction: dressed foundry yard and track, its sky, grade, fonts and kit, ambient life",
      "library fonts and .cube grades load from the game's own folder when the host serves a game",
      "The dev server config no longer imports the material library, so it loads without a built `@jgengine/core`.",
      "grade LUTs and game fonts load through the per-game asset resolver",
      "Fernwild takes its tropical sky, tropical lush grade, holo kit with the shallows-teal accent, Oswald and Source Sans 3, and lists them in its credits",
      "Harbor Heat looks like its art direction: faced city blocks, dressed streets and ground, its sky, grade, fonts and kit, ambient life",
      "static content stops paying per-frame matrix and draw cost: static matrices, batched props, HLOD per cell, on-demand capture and precompile off the critical path",
      "A far HLOD cell no longer draws a proxy and impostor cards for the same prop, and its proxy holds only a model's coarsest level instead of every level.",
      "the Rapier adapter is typed with handle maps and no per-contact scans, Rapier's character and vehicle controllers sit behind the backend seam, and games step at a fixed rate with render interpolation by default",
      "A hosted world saves at most once a second by default in the node server (`saveIntervalMs`), the memory store no longer copies a snapshot twice, radius queries skip a dedupe set, and viewer interest and entity fingerprints allocate less. 64 clients by 2,000 entities: host 110-126 ms to 58-76 ms per tick on this container, 21.9 MB to 14.1 MB allocated per tick.",
      "Drift Foundry rebuilt its career, event and calendar snapshot on every call, several times per tick: a steady-state step falls from 442 KB to 40 KB allocated and from 0.60 ms to 0.09 ms.",
